<title>PERU: Peru hunts plane missing with foreign oil workers.</title>
<headline>Peru hunts plane missing with foreign oil workers.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Peruvian Air Force hunted on Saturday for a light plane used by U.S. oil company Anadarko Petroleum Corp that has been missing since Friday with one U.S. and two Canadian men aboard.</p>
<p>An Air Force plane and helicopter were searching for the twin-motor Cessna C-404 in the district of San Roman, near the town of Pucallpa in the Amazon jungle close to Peru's border with Brazil.</p>
<p>&quot;This is where we think it disappeared, but there is no sign of anything yet,&quot; Air Force spokesman Oscar Salvador said.</p>
<p>Pucallpa airport official Martin Del Aguila identified the missing men as pilot Kent Widmer and oil engineers Pierre Moisan, both from Canada, and Clifford Bishop from the United States.</p>
<p>Other airport officials said the Cessna belonged to the Canadian airline Aerodat.</p>
</text>
